---
id: exp-docs-language-contract
title: Documentation language contract
date: 2026-05-19
primary_reaction: rxn-main
primary_result: res-main
primary_sample: sample-product
primary_analysis: ana-tlc
---

The source title is @meta.title. The primary reaction ran at @reaction.temperature.
Inline chemistry is written as :chem[CCO] in Markdown prose.

:::chemd #mol-substrate
kind: molecule
name: benzaldehyde
smiles: O=Cc1ccccc1
role: substrate
:::

:::chemd #mol-product
kind: molecule
name: benzyl alcohol
smiles: OCc1ccccc1
role: product
:::

:::chemd #rxn-main
kind: reaction
name: reduction
reactants: @mol-substrate
products: @mol-product
reagents: NaBH4
solvent: MeOH
temperature: 25 C
time: 1 h
atmosphere: nitrogen
yield: 82%
:::

:::chemd #rxn-var1
kind: reaction
name: lower temperature variant
reactants: @mol-substrate
products: @mol-product
reagents: NaBH4
solvent: MeOH
temperature: 0 C
time: 2 h
atmosphere: nitrogen
yield: 64%
:::

:::result #res-main
reaction: rxn-main
product: mol-product
status: success
yield: 82%
conversion: 94%
selectivity: 90%
isolated_mass: 120 mg
product_state: colorless oil
purity: 98%
notes: product isolated after extraction
:::

:::result #res-var1
reaction: rxn-var1
product: mol-product
status: partial
yield: 64%
conversion: 75%
purity: 92%
notes: lower temperature slowed conversion
:::

:::analysis #ana-tlc
type: tlc
ref: rxn-main
time: 1 h
eluent: petroleum ether/ethyl acetate 3:1
p1: sm 0.62
p2: rxn 0.31 ^3(4) | sm 0.62 v1
p3: product 0.30
:::

:::analysis #ana-hplc
type: hplc
ref: res-main
method: area normalization
instrument: Agilent 1260
result: 98% area product peak
data: Main peak at 6.2 min with trace impurity.
:::

:::sample #sample-crude
name: crude reaction mixture
ref: rxn-main
derived_from: rxn-main
artifacts: art-tlc
:::

:::sample #sample-product
name: purified product
ref: res-main
derived_from: sample-crude
purity: 98%
artifacts: art-nmr | art-hplc
:::

:::artifact #art-tlc
kind: tlc_image
ref: ana-tlc
path: data/tlc/main.png
instrument: phone camera
:::

:::artifact #art-nmr
kind: nmr_spectrum
ref: sample-product
path: data/nmr/product.pdf
checksum: sha256:productnmr
instrument: Bruker 400
:::

:::artifact #art-hplc
kind: hplc_report
ref: ana-hplc
path: data/hplc/product.pdf
instrument: Agilent 1260
:::

:::condition-varies #cv-temperature
standard: rxn-main
condition: solvent=MeOH | temperature=25 C | atmosphere=nitrogen
varies: temperature | time
var1: reaction=rxn-var1 | temperature=0 C | time=2 h
res1: res-var1
note1: lower temperature reduces conversion
notes: one-variable temperature screen
:::

:::procedure #proc-main
ref: rxn-main
reaction: rxn-main
evidence: notebook-page-12,art-tlc
step: charge | id=s-charge | inputs=@mol-substrate | outputs=mixture-a | evidence=notebook-page-12 | confidence=0.98
step: cool | id=s-cool | temperature=0 C | dependsOn=s-charge

:::step #s-add
family: add
stage: reaction
inputs: NaBH4
outputs: mixture-b
dependsOn: s-cool
evidence: notebook-page-12
confidence: 0.95
:::

step: heat | id=s-warm | temperature=25 C | duration=1 h | dependsOn=s-add
step: sample | id=s-sample | outputs=@sample-crude | dependsOn=s-warm
step: analyze | id=s-analyze | analysisType=tlc | dependsOn=s-sample
:::

:::observation #obs-main
ref: proc-main
event: color_change | id=e-color | value=pale-yellow | linkedStep=s-add | confidence=0.8

:::event #e-gas
type: gas_evolution
severity: low
linkedStep: s-add
evidence: notebook-page-12
confidence: 0.7
:::
:::

:::template reaction-summary
params: rxn: ref<reaction> | result: ref<result> | label: string | target: quantity<temperature>
bind: reaction=rxn-main
description: reusable reaction summary

Template @param.label resolves @param.rxn and @param.result at @param.target.
Bound reaction solvent is @reaction.solvent.
:::

:::use reaction-summary
rxn: rxn-main
result: res-main
label: main reduction
target: 25 C
:::

:::col 3
col: Left column reads @reaction.solvent and @res-main.yield.
col: {
Middle column keeps Markdown content and :chem[NaBH4].
}
col: {:::analysis #ana-col
type: tlc
ref: res-main
data: Column analysis content compiled through col child parsing.
:::
:::}
:::
